<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
    The app applicationId defines the permission and authority exported by its API:

    io.github.davelewis360.ankidroid.m3expressive.permission.xxx       - release
    io.github.davelewis360.ankidroid.m3expressive.debug.permission.xxx - debug

    Integration test builds (androidTest) run under the '.debug' application ID but
    require a working API permission for testing.

    We need <uses-permission> to grant
    'io.github.davelewis360.ankidroid.m3expressive.debug.permission.READ_WRITE_DATABASE'.

    The debug permission should not be in a release build. An androidTest-only manifest
    is ignored: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/26244998/androidmanifest-in-androidtest-directory-being-ignored

    Therefore this debug manifest is also used by androidTest.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="io.github.davelewis360.ankidroid.m3expressive.debug.permission.READ_WRITE_DATABASE"/>
</manifest>
